## Docs architecture

All documentation follows the SciAgent canonical taxonomy. Agents MUST route artifacts
to their correct location and follow the naming rules below.

### Public-facing (committed, tracked)
- docs/README.md — navigation hub
- docs/stages/ — durable per-phase methodology guides
- docs/reference/ — external dataset READMEs and data lineage

### Internal-facing (gitignored via SCIAGENT:GITIGNORE block)
- docs/_internal/reasoning/ — reasoning traces: YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_topic.md
- docs/_internal/research/  — web-research notes: YYYYMMDD_topic.md
- docs/_internal/plans/     — planning iterations
- docs/_internal/reports/   — audit/quality reports (NOT in 03_results/)
- docs/_internal/handoffs/  — handoff_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.md + MANIFEST.txt

### Naming rules (enforced by sciagent validate)
- Dated artifacts: YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_topic.md or YYYYMMDD_topic.md (snake_case only)
- Archive convention: _archive/YYYYMMDD/ per stage — never parallel .archive + _deprecated + _legacy
- No .md reports inside 03_results/ — move to docs/_internal/reports/
- Repo root holds at most: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, README.md, context.md, one current handoff
